%N A401264 Decimal expansion of the second largest volume of a polyhedron with 10 vertices inscribed in the unit sphere after that of the record-setting polyhedron described in A339262.
%C A401264 This polyhedron has 3 vertices of degree 4, 6 of degree 5, and one vertex of degree 6. The adjacency list of its graph is given by 1[2 3 4 5 6 7], 2[1 7 8 9 3], 3[1 2 9 4], 4[1 3 9 10 5], 5[1 4 10 6], 6[1 5 10 8 7], 7[1 6 8 2], 8[2 7 6 10 9], 9[2 8 10 4 3], 10[4 9 8 6 5]. Its Schoenflies symbol is C3v, dihedral symmetry of order 6. No analytical representation of the volume is known.
